<h3>Introduction</h3>

<p>The contact feedback macro places the Keysight Ask logo
onto the page linked to a popup form that will send an email.
The sender has the option of identifying themselves or not.</p>

<p>This macro is part of the toolset for setting up department
pages within Confluence</p>

<h3>Parameters</h3>
<p><strong>Form Identifier</strong>: The form identifier text is prepended to the email such that the contact person can tell which form the email came from.</p>
<p><strong>Contact Person</strong>: The username of the person who will receive the email or a valid email address.</p>
<p><strong>CC To Email</strong>: If checked and the user provides an email address, that address will be cc'd on the email.</p>
<p><strong>Image</strong>: Which image (if any) to show.</p>
<p><strong>Text</strong>: Text to display to the right of the image.</p>
<p><strong>Dialog Box Title</strong>: Text to display in the header of the feedback dialog box.</p>
<p><strong>Dialog Box Help</strong>: Text to display in the lower left corner of the feedback dialog box.</p>

<h3>Cautions</h3>
<p>Using single or double quotes in any of the fields can break
the javascript that triggers the dialog.  It is strongly recommended
to not use them.</p>

